Let's assume that the IPv4 header has already been removed from the payload, and you have the raw TCP segment in the Uint8Array.

Here's a TypeScript function to parse the basic fields of a TCP segment:
```typescript
function parseTCPSegment(tcpSegment: Uint8Array): {
  srcPort: number;
  dstPort: number;
  seqNum: number;
  ackNum: number;
  dataOffset: number;
  flags: {
    fin: boolean;
    syn: boolean;
    rst: boolean;
    psh: boolean;
    ack: boolean;
    urg: boolean;
    ece: boolean;
    cwr: boolean;
  };
  windowSize: number;
  checksum: number;
  urgentPointer: number;
} {
  const srcPort = (tcpSegment[0] << 8) | tcpSegment[1];
  const dstPort = (tcpSegment[2] << 8) | tcpSegment[3];
  const seqNum = (tcpSegment[4] << 24) | (tcpSegment[5] << 16) | (tcpSegment[6] << 8) | tcpSegment[7];
  const ackNum = (tcpSegment[8] << 24) | (tcpSegment[9] << 16) | (tcpSegment[10] << 8) | tcpSegment[11];
  const dataOffsetAndReserved = (tcpSegment[12] & 0xf0) >> 4;
  const flags = {
    fin: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x01) !== 0,
    syn: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x02) !== 0,
    rst: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x04) !== 0,
    psh: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x08) !== 0,
    ack: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x10) !== 0,
    urg: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x20) !== 0,
    ece: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x40) !== 0,
    cwr: (tcpSegment[13] & 0x80) !== 0,
  };
  const windowSize = (tcpSegment[14] << 8) | tcpSegment[15];
  const checksum = (tcpSegment[16] << 8) | tcpSegment[17];
  const urgentPointer = (tcpSegment[18] << 8) | tcpSegment[19];
  const dataOffset = dataOffsetAndReserved * 4;

  return {
    srcPort,
    dstPort,
    seqNum,
    ackNum,
    dataOffset,
    flags,
    windowSize,
    checksum,
    urgentPointer,
  };
}
```
This function will extract the source and destination ports, sequence and acknowledgement numbers, data offset, flags, window size, checksum, and urgent pointer from the TCP segment. Note that this is a simplified implementation and does not handle all possible edge cases. A full TCP stack implementation would also require handling retransmissions, congestion control, and other complex features.

